# .env.local template for book-kit v1.1.0+ multi-source research.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` at the workspace root and fill in real
# values. `.env.local` is gitignored and should NEVER be committed.
#
# Usage:
#   - The `check-search-keys.sh` helper (book-kit/bin/check-search-keys.sh)
#     sources `.env.local` and prints masked status of each key.
#   - The `parallel_search.py` orchestrator reads FIRECRAWL_API_KEY when
#     invoking the Firecrawl MCP layer (Exa is OAuth-wired and needs no key).

# Required: Firecrawl API key (for primary search)
# Sign up at https://firecrawl.dev to obtain one. The MCP server at
# https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp-oauth accepts this key via the OAuth
# flow; without it the Firecrawl layer returns an empty result list.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Optional: Exa API key (Exa MCP is also wired via OAuth at
# https://mcp.exa.ai/mcp; this is an override for direct API calls when
# the OAuth flow is unavailable).
EXA_API_KEY=
